    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (28 tests, 0 failures). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` derivation following the existing project pattern used for other read-time derived owner fields (like `membershipTier`).\n\nThe `locality` field is a **read-time derived value**, so I added it in two places that mirror how `membershipTier` works:\n\n1. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient getLocality()` getter that maps the city to its region via a fixed table (`Sydney\u2192NSW`, `Melbourne\u2192VIC`, `Brisbane\u2192QLD`), returning `\"UNKNOWN\"` for any city not in the table.\n\n2. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct auto-maps `Owner.getLocality()` \u2192 `OwnerDto.locality` in `toOwnerDto`.\n\nNo changes to the OfficeFloor YAML pipelines were needed since `locality` is computed on read (during the response mapping) rather than as a pipeline step \u2014 consistent with how `membershipTier` is derived. The `GET /api/owners/{ownerId}` response now includes `locality`, satisfying both new Cp17 tests (`Sydney \u2192 NSW`, unknown city \u2192 `UNKNOWN`) with the whole suite green.",
